Seat 2 of a 5-seat Reweighted Range Voting count, 0-5 ballots.
Seat 1 went to Wren, so each ballot now weighs 5/(5+its score for Wren).

  ballot   gave Wren   weight   Alma   Bruno
     1          5       5/10      0      0
     2          4       5/9       0      3
     3          3       5/8       1      1
     4          2       5/7       1      1
     5          1       5/6       1      5
     6          0       5/5       5      0

1. f64
     Alma  7.17261904761904745
     Bruno 7.17261904761904834
     difference 8.881784197001252e-16
     -> declares Bruno the winner of seat 2

2. exact rationals
     Alma  1205/168
     Bruno 1205/168
     -> TIE — the tiebreak rung has to run
     gcd calls: 36  — 3 per ballot-and-candidate, to build the
                    weight, scale it by the score, and add it in

3. scaled integers, everything over l = 2329089562800
     Alma  16705672161750
     Bruno 16705672161750
     -> TIE — same answer as the rationals
     gcd calls while counting: 0   (setup, once, before any ballot: 26)
     same value? true

What the scale costs in headroom. The worst a single ballot can
contribute is 5 x 5 x (l/5), so the ballot capacity is that into the type:

  seats     denoms                  scale l   max ballots i64    in i128
      1      5..10                     2520   732013653718633     1.4e34
      2      5..15                   360360     5118976599431     9.4e31
      3      5..20                232792560        7924112383     1.5e29
      4      5..25              26771144400          68905325     1.3e27
      5      5..30            2329089562800            792015     1.5e25
      6      5..35          144403552893600             12774     2.4e23
      7      5..40         5342931457063200               345     6.4e21
      8      5..45      9419588158802421600                 0     3.6e18

One million ballots at 5 seats, worst case, in i64:
     checked_mul  -> None          (the honest answer)
     wrapping_mul -> -6801296259709551616   (what a release build does if you just write `*`)
     the same product in i128 -> 11645447814000000000
